COMPARISON OF THE IC EXAMPLE WITH ITS PREVIOUS VERSION
=====================================================

System: internal conversion D1 -> D0 of TTM-1Cz, relaxed-gradient model (CAM-B3LYP/def2-SVP), data in
relaxed-gradient_model/ (D0 gradient and Hessian at the D1 geometry, derivative couplings at the D1
geometry). Settings of the example (both versions): e_trans = 15924 cm-1, sigma = 100 cm-1,
max_e = 25000 cm-1, e_bin = 1 cm-1, low_freq_approx = 300 cm-1 (30 modes classical, 126 quantum),
Morse FCFs for modes > 400 cm-1 (D = 30000 cm-1).

Previous version: examples/IC_rate_constant.py of the main branch (commit ecf3788), old module
  (conda environment restruc: organic_radical_emitters/results/RESTRUCTURE/NonRadiativeRates),
  direct folding in energy space, sensitivity analysis with run_mode_tests = True (the FCWD is
  folded anew for each omitted mode), output FCWD_contr.dat.
Current version: examples/ic/IC_rate_constant.py of the development branch, folding in Fourier space (fcwd_method = "fft"), FCWD analysis in a single call
  (fcwd_analysis = True, _fastfold.fcwd_analysis_fft), output FCWD_contr.dat in the format of the
  previous version (enhancement factors FCWD/FCWD(-k) in the columns "rel") and FCWD_analysis.dat
  (remaining FCWD in % of the full FCWD, the inverse). The current version additionally runs the
  pair analysis, the minimal mode set and the dominant final states (FCWD_analysis = True).


1. RESULTS
----------
                              previous version      current version
  NAC (cm-1)                  111.52                111.52
  k_IC harmonic (1/s)         6.474e+03             6.474e+03
  k_IC anharmonic (1/s)       1.042e+07             1.042e+07
  FCWD (1/cm), direct vs. fft folding of the current module: harmonic rel. deviation
  1.1e-08, anharmonic 4.2e-11 (FCWD: harmonic 8.797513e-13, anharmonic 1.416425e-09)

Enhancement factors FCWD/FCWD(-k) (FCWD_contr.dat, previous vs. current version):
  modes compared: 126
  FCWDh(-k) : max rel deviation 2.2e-05 (median 0.0e+00); entries identical to printed digits: 121 of 126
  FCWDh rel : max rel deviation 2.1e-05 (median 0.0e+00); entries identical to printed digits: 123 of 126
  FCWDa(-k) : max rel deviation 0.0e+00 (median 0.0e+00); entries identical to printed digits: 126 of 126
  FCWDa rel : max rel deviation 1.3e-08 (median 0.0e+00); entries identical to printed digits: 125 of 126
  largest deviation (H): 1680.87 cm-1, FCWD(-k) old 2.28891e-15 new 2.28886e-15
  top enhancement factors (H), old | new: 1681: 384.354 | 384.362, 1394: 2.764 | 2.764, 1381: 2.207 | 2.207, 1214: 1.668 | 1.668, 1010: 1.660 | 1.660
  top enhancement factors (A), old | new: 1681: 308.290 | 308.290, 1394: 1.282 | 1.282, 1381: 1.209 | 1.209, 940: 1.133 | 1.133, 1010: 1.106 | 1.106

The deviations of the harmonic values (<= 2.1e-05) occur only where omitting a mode reduces the FCWD
by orders of magnitude (1681 cm-1: FCWD(-k) ~ 2.3e-15); they are the absolute round-off of the
folding in Fourier space (~1e-19 for window averages). The anharmonic values agree to printed
precision (1e-8).

rates_new.dat (frequencies, Huang-Rhys factors, projected NACs): the previous version assigned the
NACs with a fixed offset (nacv_pf[7:]); for TTM-1Cz (6 discarded modes, no imaginary mode) every NAC
was attributed to the next higher mode and the last mode was missing (155 instead of 156 rows). The
current version selects the NACs of the modes entering the FCWD by frequency (156 rows, correct
assignment). The rate constants are not affected (they depend on the norm of the NAC vector only).


2. COMPUTATIONAL TIME (wall time, same machine)
------------------------------------------------
Complete example scripts:
  previous version, with run_mode_tests           42.39 s
  previous version, without run_mode_tests          1.10 s
  -> sensitivity analysis of the previous version   41.29 s
  current version, FCWD_analysis = True            12.48 s   (incl. pair analysis, mode sets, dominant states)

Steps of the current module:
  run_simulation, direct folding                    0.54 s
  run_simulation, Fourier space (fft)               0.42 s
  single-mode analysis, direct (as before)         39.23 s
  single-mode analysis, Fourier space              0.608 s   -> speed-up x64
  pair analysis (all pairs, Fourier space)          4.04 s
  minimal mode set (harmonic / anharmonic)          2.01 s / 2.26 s
  dominant final states (harmonic / anharmonic)     1.10 s / 1.34 s

The FCWD analysis of the previous version (single modes, 41.3 s) is reduced to 0.61 s (x64),
i.e. FCWD and single-mode analysis together take ~1.0 s instead of 42.4 s. The remaining time of the
current example is spent on the additional analyses (pairs, mode sets, dominant states).


